# Design Decisions

## Why LangGraph?

LangGraph makes the workflow explicit.

Instead of having one large chatbot function, the application separates:

```text
routing
↓
tool execution
↓
response generation
```

into individual nodes.

This makes the system easier to:

- test
- evaluate
- inspect
- modify
- reason about

---

## Why MCP?

MCP separates the conversational AI layer from backend capabilities.

The agent does not directly know how banking data is stored.

Instead:

```text
Agent
↓
MCP Client
↓
MCP Server
↓
Banking capability
```

This makes it possible to later replace the mock backend with a real API or database without redesigning the conversational workflow.

---

## Why Mock Banking Data?

The goal of this project is to demonstrate:

```text
conversational AI
+
agent orchestration
+
MCP
+
evaluation
+
voice processing
```

rather than build a complete banking backend.

The mock data layer keeps the project focused while preserving a realistic separation between the AI layer and backend capabilities.

---

## Why Structured Routing?

The router returns a Pydantic model rather than unrestricted text.

For example:

```python
class RouteDecision(BaseModel):
    route: Literal[
        "faq",
        "card_status",
        "lost_card",
        "stolen_card",
        "unknown",
    ]
```

This makes routing:

- deterministic in format
- easier to test
- easier to evaluate
- safer than parsing arbitrary model output

---

# Key Engineering Takeaways

This project demonstrates:

- building controlled conversational workflows with LangGraph
- exposing backend capabilities through MCP
- using structured LLM output for routing
- separating customer-specific tools from general FAQs
- grounding responses in trusted backend data
- preventing unsupported action claims
- evaluating routing separately from response quality
- using evaluation failures to improve routing behavior
- integrating STT and TTS without modifying the core agent
- measuring end-to-end conversational latency
- testing robustness when speech transcription is imperfect

